# panelgothic
#
# The house face. A single stroke gothic drawn for a 0.4 mm tip cutter at
# 3 mm cap height, which is the size most of the legend work goes out at.
#
# Design grid is 1000 units to the em with the capitals at 700. Curves are
# polylines because the cutter follows polylines; the point spacing was
# picked so the chord error is under a hundredth of a millimetre at 3 mm.
#
# Rules that were followed while drawing this and should be followed by
# anyone editing it:
#
#   - No two strokes in a glyph come closer than 90 units except where they
#     deliberately meet. At 3 mm that is 0.39 mm, which clears a 0.4 mm tip
#     at the depth this face is cut at.
#   - Counters stay open. The e is drawn with a bar that stops short rather
#     than a closed eye, because a closed eye fills in on the second pass.
#   - Terminals stop on a coordinate, never on a curve tangent, so a glyph
#     can be split and rejoined without moving.

face panelgothic
upem 1000
cap 700
xheight 500
ascender 750
descender -200
linegap 100
fallback question

